“اَلْاَنْفُ” (al-anf): the nose, or tip, the strongest and hardest part of something, which is in the front. {T}{R}

5:45 And the nose for nose
وَالأَنفَ بِالأَنفِ

“اَلْاِسْتِنَافُ” (al-istenafu): to begin something new. {T}{R}

The Arabs apply both wealth and disgrace to it. As “حَمِيَ اَنْفُهُ” (hamiya anfahu): that he became respected, and “رَغِمَ اَنْفُهُ” (raghema anfahu) he became disgraced: {M}.

“اَنِفًا” (anefan): “just now”. The Quran uses this meaning in 47:16.
